nio: publish static personalities after all IOKit subsystems init

Run 678 moved nio_publish_static_personalities() to just after
IOCatalogue::initialize() in iokit_post_constructor_init, to get the
personalities into the catalogue before the lockdown matching sweep. That
spot is too early: the 19:50 photograph shows a kernel data abort with
pc = IOCatalogue::~IOCatalogue()+0x4 and frames in addDrivers(),
exchangeDrivers(), findDrivers() and isModuleLoaded(). addDrivers() at
that point runs before OSKext::initialize() and the other subsystems have
run, so the catalogue's class symbols / kext environment are not ready.

Move the call to the end of iokit_post_constructor_init, after every
initialize() and IOPMinformeeList's lock. The catalogue, class symbols and
kext environment are then ready, and this is still long before
PE_lockdown_iokit() runs its sweep, so both the lockdown sweep and the
later StartIOKitMatching sweep see the personalities. The function's
static bool keeps publication to once.

diff --git a/iokit/Kernel/IOStartIOKit.cpp b/iokit/Kernel/IOStartIOKit.cpp
--- a/iokit/Kernel/IOStartIOKit.cpp
+++ b/iokit/Kernel/IOStartIOKit.cpp
@@ -107,14 +107,6 @@ iokit_post_constructor_init(void)
 	assert( root );
 	IOService::initialize();
 	IOCatalogue::initialize();
-	/* nio: publish the static drivers' personalities here, before the
-	 * lockdown. PE_lockdown_iokit() runs its matching sweep before bsd_init()
-	 * and reads the catalogue as it is then; the only surviving call sat in
-	 * StartIOKitMatching(), which runs after the lockdown. So the lockdown
-	 * sweep never saw NioUfs (nor the platform expert), no driver attached,
-	 * and start() was never entered. Publishing here makes both sweeps see
-	 * the same catalogue; the static bool in the function makes it once. */
-	nio_publish_static_personalities();
 	IOStatistics::initialize();
 	OSKext::initialize();
 	IOUserClient::initialize();
@@ -125,6 +117,15 @@ iokit_post_constructor_init(void)
 	// Initializes IOPMinformeeList class-wide shared lock
 	IOPMinformeeList::getSharedRecursiveLock();
 
+	/* nio: publish the static drivers' personalities before the lockdown
+	 * sweep, but only AFTER every IOKit subsystem above is initialized.
+	 * Calling addDrivers() right after IOCatalogue::initialize() (the earlier
+	 * attempt) data-aborted in IOCatalogue::addDrivers/isModuleLoaded:
+	 * OSKext::initialize() and the rest had not run yet. Here the catalogue,
+	 * the class symbols and the kext environment are all ready, and this is
+	 * still long before PE_lockdown_iokit() runs its matching sweep. */
+	nio_publish_static_personalities();
+
 	obj = OSString::withCString( version );
 	assert( obj );
 	if (obj) {
